4. EXPERIENCE CONTRACT (design everything to this)
=====================================================
GUEST
* Portal opens in <=2.5 s on throttled 3G: initial payload <=100 KB gzipped, zero third-party requests, media lazy-loaded.
* Free path: consent + ad -> internet in <=3 taps after choosing Free. Paid path: <=5 taps. After verified payment: internet within 5 s, automatically.
* Every state is designed, in Sesotho and English, with plain-language text and a next step (no raw codes): loading, portal unreachable, payment pending (with reassurance and a "check status" button), payment failed, paid but login failed, expired, device limit reached, already connected, ad failed (policy fallback), RADIUS/app degraded.
* After login: status page with time/data left, an expiry warning 10 minutes before the end, one-tap renew, and "recover my access" using phone + reference/PIN. A paid user can add a device within the plan's device limit without paying again.
* Recovery of an interrupted payment is server-side (by an unguessable per-session token), never browser storage, because captive sheets wipe it.

ADMIN
* Add router: live adoption progress (token issued, handshake, tunnel up, RADIUS ok, hotspot ok, walled garden ok) with per-step failure hints and a copy-paste one-liner. Target: first router online in under 10 minutes.
* Every policy or mode change shows an impact preview ("affects N routers, M active sessions; effective immediately / next session"), asks for confirmation, is audited, and can be undone.
* Conflict warnings: Free mode with no ad or limits, gateway enabled but its domain missing from the walled garden, router in drift, router offline.
* Support lookup: one search box (phone, MAC, PIN, transaction reference) shows a single timeline of payment, voucher, entitlement, RADIUS auth/accounting and router status, with audited actions (re-verify, retry fulfilment, manual grant, kick).
* Dashboards: live sessions, revenue per router/group/partner, conversion funnel (splash -> select -> pay -> success), ad performance, router health, reconciliation status, alerts. CSV/PDF exports respect scope. Per-partner revenue-share statements.

